  "$comment": "Adversarial Ed25519 signature forms for at.opake.publicKey account binding. Single source of truth, consumed by opake-core (Rust, compile time) and the indexer (Elixir, test boot) so both verifiers are held to one accept/reject boundary. Vectors are derived from the signing key seed 42 repeated 32 times: `valid_signature` is a genuine signature over the message, `noncanonical_s` adds the group order L to its S, `low_order_r` zeroes its R, `signature_over_a_different_message` signs the message plus a trailing full stop, and the identity-point vectors pair a small-order key with a small-order R and S = 0 — the forgery OTP's :crypto.verify accepts for any transcript. `smallOrderPointsHex` lists every encoding of the eight small-order points, including the non-canonical spellings a decoder reducing modulo p accepts.",
